#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:213
msgid ""
"Configure the current range filter (IRF) type which determines the filtering"
" mechanism applied on current range changes. We do not recommend changing "
"these settings for normal operation."
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:216
msgid ""
"\"interp\" is the default setting which interpolates over the samples in the"
" window using the value computed by the pre and post values. This gives the "
"most intuitive behavior."
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:219
msgid ""
"\"mean\" sets all samples in the window to the mean value. This results in a"
" straight horizontal line that allows you to clearly see current range "
"changes while still providing the best long-term current range measurement."
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:223
msgid "\"NaN\" sets all samples in the window to NaN."
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:224
msgid ""
"\"off\" disables the current range filtering, and you will see additional "
"current range switching artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:236
msgid "IRF pre"
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:237
msgid ""
"The number of samples before the current range window used to determine the "
"mean. This value is ignored for all other IRF types."
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:245
msgid "IRF window"
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:246
msgid ""
"Use \"n\" for automatic duration based upon known response time. Use \"m\" "
"for shorter automatic duration that may result in min/max distortion. Use "
"any other value to specify a fixed, manual window duration in samples."
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:254
msgid "IRF post"
msgstr ""

#: devices/jsdrv/js110.py:255
msgid ""
"The number of samples after the current range window used to determine the "
"mean. This value is ignored for all other IRF types."
msgstr ""

